# BUG-469: `Timer()` -- a runtime object type called like a constructor it does not have --
# reached Zig as "use of undeclared identifier 'Timer'", and because `t` was then untyped
# the misspelled `t.elapsedMs()` was never refused either. Ten more runtime types had the
# same gap (measured; see runtimeFactoryHint). The refusal names the documented factory.
def main()
    var t = Timer()
    print(t.elapsed())
